              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@899",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@901",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@903",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@905"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "intro.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "intro.p04.01",
            "text": "The book opens with foundations.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p04.02",
            "text": "Chapter 1 introduces what LLMs are, why building them from scratch is valuable, how generative AI and the broader AI stack relate to them, what modern systems do, and why transformers are central.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p04.03",
            "text": "It also lays out the build pipeline from stage one to stage three, while making explicit where prerequisite coverage is partial and where evidence gaps remain.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p04.04",
            "text": "Chapter 2 then turns raw text into model inputs by moving from word tokenization to character and subword methods, bringing in byte pair encoding, embeddings, positional information, and the full preprocessing pipeline needed to create next-token training examples.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p04.05",
            "text": "Chapter 3 builds directly on those representations and develops the transformer’s core mechanics: self-attention, causal masking, multi-head attention, layer normalization, residual pathways, and the implementation details that make contextual representations possible.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "intro.p05",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "intro.p05.01",
            "text": "With those building blocks in place, the book assembles complete models and then adapts them to practical settings.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p05.02",
            "text": "Chapter 4 constructs a full GPT-style model, defines next-token prediction, trains it in a pretraining loop, and shows how generation changes under greedy decoding, temperature, and top-k sampling.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p05.03",
            "text": "Chapter 5 moves from training from scratch to using pretrained GPT-2 weights, mapping released parameters into the architecture and then fine-tuning the model for spam classification with padded datasets, dataloaders, and accuracy-based evaluation.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p05.04",
            "text": "Chapter 6 extends that workflow to instruction fine-tuning, covering prompt formatting, variable-length batching, shifted targets, masking choices in the loss, loading pretrained weights again, and evaluating instruction-following behavior with both examples and broader benchmarking ideas.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "intro.p05.05",
            "text": "By the end, each chapter has built on the one before it: from concepts, to inputs, to transformer internals, to GPT pretraining, to transfer, and finally to instruction-following systems.",
            "type": "R",
            "cites": []
          }
        ]
      }
